WEBVTT

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.799
So would love to kind of know about this

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:06.240
whole concept of personal cash flow. So

00:00:04.799 --> 00:00:08.559
a lot of people who may be listening

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:11.120
today may not know about cash flow and

00:00:08.559 --> 00:00:12.880
how they can leverage a boring business

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:14.880
to kind of create this personal cash

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:16.480
flow for themselves. So what would you

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.880
say to somebody that's starting out

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:20.640
today who wants to start building out

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:22.960
some personal cash flow? What kind of

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:24.560
business or what what would you say to

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:27.680
them? Like what is your advice for the

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:30.560
younger you? I would say start with the

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:33.360
end in mind and do a a serious analysis

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:35.520
of how much cash you actually need to

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:38.000
have freedom to do what you want to do.

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:39.920
Too many entrepreneurs, they set the bar

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.760
at building a billion-doll company or

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:43.440
making a hund00 million or doing

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:46.239
whatever or they don't even have a goal

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:48.480
in mind at all. But I like the practice

00:00:46.239 --> 00:00:50.879
of getting in and looking at what you

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:53.280
need as an entrepreneur to live the life

00:00:50.879 --> 00:00:55.280
you want to live. Like start with that

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:57.199
goal in mind. And when I was in 20 in

00:00:55.280 --> 00:01:00.480
2012 when I did this exercise a year out

00:00:57.199 --> 00:01:03.199
of college, I realized I wanted $20,000

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:04.640
a month coming in and I could live the

00:01:03.199 --> 00:01:06.640
life of my dreams. Many areas in the

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:08.320
world are much more affordable, but I

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:10.240
was living in Boston. I wanted to have a

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:11.600
safe vehicle for my family. I wanted to

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:12.640
have a decent apartment or house. I

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:13.840
wanted to be able to play golf at a

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:15.840
country club. I wanted to be able to do

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:18.720
these things. I want to be able to go um

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:20.080
look at a menu at a restaurant and order

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:21.520
without worrying about the price. Little

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:23.840
things like that that could make me be

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:27.040
able to live the life I wanted to live.

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:29.360
and set a number. My number was $20,000

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:31.520
a month. So then I stood stood back and

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:33.040
unemotionally, it didn't matter what I

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:35.200
wanted. It wasn't selfish. It was not it

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:37.600
was not about me. I said, "What's the

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:40.079
thing that I can do that increased my

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:42.640
odds of achieving that goal, $20,000 a

00:01:40.079 --> 00:01:44.640
month, and how can I increase the odds

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:46.960
and and play the game that's more likely

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:50.560
to get me to where I want to be?" So, I

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:52.320
think setting a personal cash flow goal

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:54.560
is something that so few entrepreneurs

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:56.079
actually do and it impacts their

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:58.000
decision-m. If you want to you want to

00:01:56.079 --> 00:01:59.680
make a billion dollars, then yes, go go

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.520
try to change the world. You need to

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:02.560
have a major a big company. You need to

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:04.560
go public. You need to have an

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:07.280
acquisition. But if you want to live the

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:10.080
life you want to live, sometimes it's a

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:12.400
totally different approach.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:15.440
>> Yeah, I think that's a really good kind

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:17.360
of pro and con kind of analogy over

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:19.120
there. And uh so I would just love to

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:22.560
know like who are the founders that

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:25.440
you're betting big on in 2025 and what

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:29.280
is it that you know kind of attracts

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:31.920
them you to like want to root for them

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:33.840
support them and like yeah just like

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:35.519
what is the archetype of founders that

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:36.720
you support and you kind of rally

00:02:35.519 --> 00:02:40.080
behind?

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:42.239
>> I think as as a startup you have a

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:44.400
disadvantage in almost every area of

00:02:42.239 --> 00:02:46.879
business. Your competitors have more

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:48.800
cash, they have more marketing, they

00:02:46.879 --> 00:02:50.720
have better sales, they have more brand

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:52.160
awareness, they get more referrals, they

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:53.519
have a, you know, they have an

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:55.519
infrastructure and a company in place

00:02:53.519 --> 00:02:57.440
that creates money every every month.

00:02:55.519 --> 00:02:58.800
And that's a massive advantage. All

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:00.239
those things are big advantages. They

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:01.680
can afford to spend more on marketing.

00:03:00.239 --> 00:03:03.440
They can afford to hire people. They can

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:06.000
afford to do all the things that you

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:09.680
can't afford to do as a founder.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:11.280
Your one advantage is speed.

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:12.879
You can make decisions in the morning

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:15.519
and they can be in place inside your

00:03:12.879 --> 00:03:18.080
business before lunch. And if you can

00:03:15.519 --> 00:03:20.080
move very fast and you can test and you

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:22.720
can try and you can go sell and you can

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:24.319
experiment, then you are way way more

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:25.760
likely to win. And it's it's frankly

00:03:24.319 --> 00:03:28.159
your only advantage in the early days.

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:30.000
So I stay away from people who

00:03:28.159 --> 00:03:32.080
overanalyze.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.200
Meaning like I'm going to study study

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:38.640
study aim aim aim aim aim aim aim aim

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:41.200
shoot. I like founders who get out, mix

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:43.760
it up, try to make money. Shoot, aim,

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:45.760
shoot, aim, shoot, shoot, shoot, aim,

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:48.239
shoot, shoot, shoot, aim. That makes

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:48.239
sense.

